# An element that is not there is undefined, and every relation with undefined fails. A relation that FAILED cuts its subject only where the other side is a number whatever runs:
# a constant, a parameter or a variable that is declared, what is computed from those, what stands behind a promise. What a cast alone states of a read cuts nothing there. THE LYING CONTROLS: each is reported
# round: the failed `>=` on the way round a loop . front: the same in front of a step . sum: undefined + 1 is NaN, and NaN fails as well
# THE RIGHT ONES: held: the relation HOLDS: then both sides are numbers . limit: a declared parameter . kept, left: behind a promise stands an int32, though only the walk proves that promise; the one call in sight passes a text
